## The decision on the fold test (a byte copy or a build)

The r6-v3 fold test holds a different lead page: its page 1 extracts as "ip on long edge", and a
fresh lead build extracts as "flip on long edge" (the fl ligature has no ToUnicode map in the older
file). The two rasters differ in 90 pixels at 100 dpi, at most 8 grey levels, inside one 16 x 21 px
box (`p9c-proof-pages.txt`). So the byte copy of the r6-v3 fold test was not used. The file is
built from the v20 book. This is not a defect of the print: both files print "flip".

